  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding of Alaska Medicaid Mayzent (siponimod), an S1P receptor modulator. Version: 2; Original: 7/05/2019; Approval: 09/16/2022; Effective: 11/01/2022.",
    "Encoded: approval criteria 1-8 and denial criteria 1-3 (failure to meet approval criteria is handled by the approval predicates). Baseline workup, cardiovascular history, genetic testing, prior therapy and skin examination are attestations.",
    "Duration (notes only): initial approval up to 3 months; reauthorization approval up to 12 months.",
    "Quantity (notes only): 120 tablets of 0.25 mg, 30 tablets of 1 mg, or 30 tablets of 2 mg per month. No numeric quantity enforcement.",
    "Cautions (notes only): increased infection risk; increased macular edema risk with history of uveitis or diabetes mellitus; bradyarrhythmia and atrioventricular conduction delays; avoid live attenuated vaccines for up to 4 weeks after treatment; concomitant moderate CYP2C9 and moderate to strong CYP3A4 inhibitors and inducers not recommended; increased risk of cutaneous malignancies.",
    "PDL status unknown: PDF is silent. MS peer alternatives require separate eligibility evaluation.",
    "Remaining gaps: documentation verification, authorization duration, reauthorization, dosing, quantity enforcement and cautions require manual review."
  ],
